.SH "NAME"
pcre2_substring_number_from_name \- convert captured string name to number
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.ss \n[.ss]
.nf
.fam C
\fB\&#include\fP \fB<pcre2.h>\fP

\fBint\fP pcre2_substring_number_from_name(\fBconst\fP \fBpcre2_code\fP *\fIcode\fP,
                                     \fBPCRE2_SPTR\fP \fIstringname\fP);
.fam
.fi
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
This convenience function finds the number of a named substring capturing
parenthesis in a compiled pattern, provided that it is a unique name. The
function arguments are:
.sp
.RS 4
.PD 0
.TP 11
\fIcode\fP
.ad l
Compiled regular expression
.TP 11
\fIstringname\fP
.ad l
Name whose number is required
.PD
.RE
.PP
.ad l
.sp
The yield of the function is the number of the parenthesis if the name is
found, or \fBPCRE2_ERROR_NOSUBSTRING\fP if it is not found. When duplicate names are
allowed (\fBPCRE2_DUPNAMES\fP is set), if the name is not unique,
\fBPCRE2_ERROR_NOUNIQUESUBSTRING\fP is returned. You can obtain the list of numbers
with the same name by calling pcre2_substring_nametable_scan().
.sp
There is a complete description of the PCRE2 native API in the
\f(CRpcre2api\fP
page and a description of the POSIX API in the
\f(CRpcre2posix\fP
page.